    "created_at": "2016-02-24T00:39:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-24T00:39:38Z",
    "body": "This doesn't affect your processor at all, and HTML already 8 other instances of `data-dfn-for`.  (And ideally this would not be Bikeshed-specific if any other preprocessors ever gain meaningful cross-spec linking capabilities; they'd use the same definition API.)\n\nI'm not comfortable with adding yet another dimension to Bikeshed's data model when it's not necessary; I already have a namespacing mechanism for uniquely identifying definitions in a human-readable manner.  Disambiguating by ID is nearly just supplying an explicit link; the only benefit would be that you don't have to write out the full spec url.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
